/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * SYNTHETIC, not lifted from a real file. A four-edge spelling of the same
 * seam, needed to reach the state codex describes in the P1 on
 * bldrs-ai/conway#609: an edge that fails to extract while the REMAINING
 * paired edges still supply three or more boundary points.
 *
 * The real #50626 above cannot reach it - its loop has a single EDGE_CURVE,
 * so failing that curve empties the boundary and the native
 * "< MINIMUM_TRIM_POINTS" guard already rejects it.
 *
 * The great circle #18104 (radius 0.9, in the plane z = 0) is split at
 * (0, 0.9, 0) into two quarter arcs, and the loop walks them out and back:
 *   A .T.  B .T.  B .F.  A .F.
 * so it is a genuine retrace - every edge exactly twice, opposite senses.
 *
 * B rides a DUPLICATE circle entity (#900010, same placement and radius) so
 * a test can fail B's extraction without touching A's.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
